## Complete Command Reference: All-in-One Cheat Sheet

### Reconnaissance Commands

```bash
# Port Scanning
cd ~/hacking-toolkit/recon

# Basic scan
python3 port_scanner.py 192.168.1.1 -p 22,80,443

# Full scan
python3 port_scanner.py 192.168.1.1 -p 1-65535 -t 100 -T 1.0

# With banners
python3 port_scanner.py 192.168.1.1 -p 22,80,443 --banners

# Save results
python3 port_scanner.py 192.168.1.1 -p 22,80,443 -o scan.json

# Quick presets
python3 quick_scan.py 192.168.1.1 web
python3 quick_scan.py 192.168.1.1 common
python3 quick_scan.py 192.168.1.1 all 200

# Packet sniffing
sudo python3 sniffer.py eth0

# Packet crafting
sudo python3 packet_crafter.py

# Network relay
python3 network_relay.py -l 8080 -t example.com -p 80 --log

# Subdomain enumeration
python3 subdomain_enum.py example.com -t 50
```

### Web Attack Commands

```bash
cd ~/hacking-toolkit/web-attack

# Directory brute force
python3 brute_forcer.py https://example.com -w common -t 30

# With extensions
python3 brute_forcer.py https://example.com -w common -e .php,.html -t 50

# Recursive
python3 brute_forcer.py https://example.com -w common -r -d 2

# Custom wordlist
python3 brute_forcer.py https://example.com -w custom.txt -t 100

# Wordlist generation
python3 wordlist_generator.py

# HTML analysis
python3 html_analyzer.py

# Authentication testing
python3 auth_automation.py --login https://example.com/login -u admin -p password
python3 auth_automation.py --bruteforce https://example.com/login --users users.txt --passwords pass.txt
```

